WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.916 --> 00:00:03.617
Jenny landed on the sidewalk with a thud.

2
00:00:04.257 --> 00:00:07.358
The lady's little dog barked and barked.

3
00:00:07.378 --> 00:00:08.358
"Oh dear!

4
00:00:08.518 --> 00:00:10.138
Are you all right?"

5
00:00:10.158 --> 00:00:10.979
cried the lady.

6
00:00:11.279 --> 00:00:15.180
Josh helped Jenny stand up.

7
00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:33.782
Her knee was skinned, and she looked stunned.

8
00:00:36.144 --> 00:00:39.467
"I'm okay," she said, brushing herself off.

9
00:00:39.487 --> 00:00:43.891
"I guess I just didn't see the dog's leash."

10
00:00:45.232 --> 00:00:48.474
Once I was sure that Jenny was all right, I looked at Molly again.

11
00:00:48.494 --> 00:00:52.237
"So can I borrow your flower?"

12
00:00:53.258 --> 00:00:54.499
This time Molly nodded.

13
00:00:54.519 --> 00:00:58.102
"I made up my mind," she said.

14
00:00:58.122 --> 00:00:59.804
"You can borrow it."

15
00:01:00.984 --> 00:01:02.505
"Wow, thanks!"

16
00:01:02.965 --> 00:01:03.365
I said.

17
00:01:03.385 --> 00:01:05.886
"I promise to take good care of it."

18
00:01:07.587 --> 00:01:11.209
When we got to Molly's apartment, she took the flower off her headband.

19
00:01:12.149 --> 00:01:13.490
Then she handed it to me.

20
00:01:13.510 --> 00:01:17.711
"I'm going home right now to try my new invention on my mom!"

21
00:01:18.072 --> 00:01:18.512
I said.

22
00:01:18.532 --> 00:01:20.232
"Good luck!"

23
00:01:20.573 --> 00:01:23.234
called Molly as I ran across the hall to my apartment.

24
00:01:25.795 --> 00:01:28.136
At home my brother, Tate, was using the computer.

25
00:01:29.096 --> 00:01:31.598
My mom was in the kitchen, making meatloaf for dinner.

26
00:01:31.618 --> 00:01:34.301
"Guess what, Mom," I said.

27
00:01:34.321 --> 00:01:37.603
"I have an idea for a great new invention!"

28
00:01:37.623 --> 00:01:42.087
"Uh-oh," said Tate, looking up from the computer.

29
00:01:42.107 --> 00:01:44.789
"He's going to make a big mess."

30
00:01:47.231 --> 00:01:48.352
My mom winked at me.

31
00:01:48.372 --> 00:01:51.495
"That's wonderful, Iggy," she said.

32
00:01:51.515 --> 00:01:54.297
"Can I borrow your reading glasses?"

33
00:01:54.717 --> 00:01:55.198
I asked.

34
00:01:55.218 --> 00:01:58.937
"They're on the kitchen table," my mom replied.

35
00:01:58.957 --> 00:02:01.780
"Please be careful with them though.

36
00:02:02.981 --> 00:02:04.843
I can't read a thing without them."

37
00:02:06.344 --> 00:02:10.168
I took Molly's flower and my mom's glasses into my room.

38
00:02:12.189 --> 00:02:15.633
Carefully, I unwound the wire stem of the flower.

39
00:02:16.674 --> 00:02:19.516
Then I wrapped it around the frames of my mom's glasses.

40
00:02:20.537 --> 00:02:23.400
The pink flower stood up, bright and tall.

41
00:02:24.572 --> 00:02:28.536
My mom would never lose her reading glasses with that flower attached to them!

42
00:02:28.556 --> 00:02:32.040
Then I realized something.

43
00:02:33.061 --> 00:02:36.104
My mom never loses her reading glasses anyway.

44
00:02:37.045 --> 00:02:38.787
She always puts them on the kitchen table.

45
00:02:39.888 --> 00:02:44.373
How was I going to test out my new invention if my mom never lost her glasses?

46
00:02:45.434 --> 00:02:46.976
That was a problem I could solve.

47
00:02:50.164 --> 00:02:51.065
After all, Mrs.

48
00:02:51.125 --> 00:02:54.627
Romano had said that inventors are problem solvers, right?

49
00:02:54.647 --> 00:03:00.069
"Iggy!" my mom called, "I need my glasses for a minute.

50
00:03:00.110 --> 00:03:01.770
I have to check something in my cookbook!

51
00:03:01.790 --> 00:03:05.713
"Okay, Mom," I said, walking into the kitchen.

52
00:03:05.733 --> 00:03:09.635
"But first you have to find your glasses."

53
00:03:11.075 --> 00:03:12.076
"What are you talking about?"

54
00:03:12.416 --> 00:03:13.257
asked my mom.

55
00:03:13.277 --> 00:03:15.958
"You just took them into your room."

56
00:03:15.978 --> 00:03:21.513
"I know," I said, "but now I'm going to hide them."

57
00:03:22.674 --> 00:03:23.975
My mom looked puzzled.

58
00:03:23.995 --> 00:03:26.176
"Is this some kind of game?"

59
00:03:26.196 --> 00:03:28.637
"No," I said.

60
00:03:28.657 --> 00:03:33.840
"But I want to test my new Fabulous Glasses-Finder invention.

61
00:03:34.921 --> 00:03:38.643
And I can't test it unless you lose your glasses."

62
00:03:38.663 --> 00:03:44.866
"That's the dumbest thing I've ever heard," called Tate from the living room.

63
00:03:44.886 --> 00:03:48.328
"Well, okay," said my mom.

64
00:03:49.516 --> 00:03:51.277
"But I don't have much time.

65
00:03:51.397 --> 00:03:52.897
I'm in the middle of preparing dinner."

66
00:03:53.958 --> 00:03:54.578
I grinned.

67
00:03:54.598 --> 00:03:57.319
"It won't take long," I said.

68
00:03:57.339 --> 00:04:02.120
"The Fabulous Glasses-Finder is my best invention yet."

69
00:04:02.140 --> 00:04:04.941
"Don't believe him, Mom!"

70
00:04:05.461 --> 00:04:06.242
said Tate.

71
00:04:06.262 --> 00:04:09.323
"You're never going to see your glasses again!"

72
00:04:10.943 --> 00:04:12.704
I told my mom to cover her eyes.

73
00:04:20.984 --> 00:04:23.366
Then I hid her glasses on a chair in her bedroom.

74
00:04:24.547 --> 00:04:28.110
That's the kind of place where someone might leave their glasses by mistake.

75
00:04:28.130 --> 00:04:29.891
"Okay, Mom!"

76
00:04:30.332 --> 00:04:32.293
I said, "You can start looking now!"

77
00:04:35.256 --> 00:04:38.519
It took my mom only three minutes to find her glasses.

78
00:04:39.780 --> 00:04:43.362
It was very easy to spot them with Molly's pink flower sticking up.

79
00:04:44.784 --> 00:04:48.226
My mom picked up her glasses and looked curiously at the flower.

80
00:04:48.247 --> 00:04:50.793
"Well," she said.

81
00:04:50.813 --> 00:04:53.478
"I must say, Iggy.

82
00:04:54.399 --> 00:04:56.683
This is a very clever idea."

83
00:04:56.703 --> 00:04:59.187
"Did you hear that, Tate?"

84
00:04:59.708 --> 00:05:00.269
I shouted.

85
00:05:00.289 --> 00:05:04.555
"My Fabulous Glasses-Finder really works!"
